    answer: "It expires 60 seconds after the function timeout, counted from when Appwrite creates the execution. A function with a 180-second timeout gets a JWT that lasts 240 seconds. The JWT is also tied to the user's session: after the user signs out, requests with it act as a guest, so reads return no rows and writes fail with a 401 error."
